    "body": "<!-- pr-reviewer: ae39b16f908ed190a4fc68d1d91deda82d46e9d9 -->\n**Review (M3, independent of the author): Ready for the maintainer to merge.**\n\n**What changed:** test-only. `the_library_folder_is_the_override_else_a_sibling_of_machines` now picks host-native absolute paths, using the same `cfg!(windows)` pattern as `machine_edit.rs`'s `user_dir_for` test. It builds the expected paths with `PathBuf::join` instead of slash-joined strings. The library code is untouched, and the assertions are the same claims with host-correct paths.\n\n**Why it was failing:** a POSIX `/shop/fixtures` isn't absolute on Windows. The author reports the Windows 11 ARM failure on main (#723's panic) and the pass on this branch.\n\n**Gate:** quick gate on Linux, `app fixture_library`: ok. I did not build or run it on Windows myself.\n\nRequested changes: none.",
